{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information involves the low-probability outcomes in both lotteries, where outcomes with probability below 20% receive a subjectively increased weight (by 10 percentage points). In this case, both lotteries have probabilities well below 20%: Lottery A has a 0.2% chance of winning 3000 Euros, and Lottery B has a 0.1% chance of winning 6000 Euros. Under the decision reason, these probabilities are subjectively transformed: 0.2% becomes 10.2% and 0.1% becomes 10.1%. The weighted outcomes are then calculated: for A, 3000 × 10.2% = 306; for B, 6000 × 10.1% = 606. The reason prefers the lottery with the higher weighted outcome, which is B. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied and would lead to choosing B.",
